WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.440
This heavy iron pendulum swings in a
smooth, predictable arc.

2
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.280
For centuries, this was the model for the
entire cosmos,

3
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:13.360
a single unified machine governed by one
set of rules

4
00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.400
that could explain everything from a
falling apple to the

5
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.640
orbits of distant planets.

6
00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:22.160
As our measurements reached the extremes
of the very large

7
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.120
and the very small, that model failed.

8
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.640
Modern physics shows that the universe
does not follow one

9
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:29.760
set of rules.

10
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.200
It follows two.

11
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:36.240
We describe our reality using two distinct
languages, general relativity

12
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.760
for the massive scale of galaxies and
quantum mechanics for

13
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.240
the subatomic scale of particles.

14
00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.800
Both theories are mathematically precise
and have survived every experimental

15
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.320
test we've thrown at them.

16
00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:52.240
They are the most accurate models humans
have ever constructed.

17
00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:54.720
The tension lies in their intersection.

18
00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.960
Despite being individually perfect, these
two models contradict each other

19
00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:00.000
at a structural level.

20
00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.560
The geometric rules we use to calculate
the movement of

21
00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:07.000
stars cannot be applied to the behavior of
atoms.

22
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.400
They are mutually untranslatable.

23
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.120
We are living in a universe that appears
to operate

24
00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:16.440
on two different, valid grammars that
cannot be combined, leaving

25
00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:19.160
us to wonder if we have actually grasped
the nature

26
00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:20.760
of reality at all.

27
00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:23.480
To see where the conflict begins, we have
to look

28
00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:27.000
at the first grammar, the physics of the
very large.

29
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.400
In general relativity, gravity is a
continuous geometric language.

30
00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.200
It isn't a force that pulls, it's the
shape of

31
00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.800
the environment itself.

32
00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:39.880
Wheeler noted the dialogue: matter tells
space how to curve,

33
00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.280
space tells matter how to move.

34
00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:46.520
This smooth geometry shatters at the
subatomic scale, replaced by

35
00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.760
discrete, vibrating data points.

36
00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:53.080
Particles inhabit multiple positions at
the same time, a superposition

37
00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:54.760
of overlapping possibilities.

38
00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.320
This grammar is defined by its refusal to
commit.

39
00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:02.240
A particle exists as a range of
probabilities until an

40
00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:06.720
interaction forces it to settle into a
single definitive state.

41
00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:11.200
Reality functions through smooth dialogue
at the cosmic scale and

42
00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.000
chaotic abundance at the microscale.

43
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.600
These two grammars work perfectly, but
only if they never

44
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:19.920
have to occupy the same page.

45
00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.880
But there are places where the universe
forces these two

46
00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:26.560
grammars together. At the center of a
black hole, an

47
00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:30.400
immense mass is crushed into a subatomic
space.

48
00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.120
When we try to use both theories to
describe a

49
00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.840
singularity, the math breaks.

50
00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:39.840
The equations for gravity and the
equations for particles collide

51
00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.080
and collapse into paradox.

52
00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:45.200
This creates a total breakdown in our
description of the

53
00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.360
physical world. To resolve it, we need a
mathematical framework

54
00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:53.000
capable of reconciling these contradictory
behaviors.

55
00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:57.160
Theories like string theory or loop
quantum gravity are attempts

56
00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:00.680
to build that framework, seeking a single
set of equations

57
00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:03.400
that can describe both the curve of a
galaxy and

58
00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.240
the vibration of an atom.

59
00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:08.520
The fact that our best theories fail at
these extremes

60
00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.480
suggests they aren't the final word on
reality.

61
00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:14.840
They are likely just footnotes to a
deeper, more complex

62
00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.240
story we haven't yet learned how to read.

63
00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:20.760
This crisis in translation has pushed some
physicists to look

64
00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.640
away from the equations and focus on the
person writing

65
00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.160
them, the observer.

66
00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:29.080
We often view ourselves as passive
witnesses, watching the universe

67
00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:31.480
from behind an objective pane of glass.

68
00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.960
Quantum mechanics suggests otherwise.

69
00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:36.840
At the subatomic level, the act of looking
at a

70
00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:40.280
system is an intervention that changes the
system's state.

71
00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:42.440
This is the process of selection.

72
00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:45.000
Measurement doesn't reveal a hidden
reality.

73
00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:48.880
It forces a cloud of quantum possibilities
to collapse into

74
00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:50.160
a single choice.

75
00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:53.600
If the act of observation defines the
outcome, then our

76
00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:57.360
search for a perfectly objective theory is
inherently limited.

77
00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:01.360
We cannot find a neutral, outside
perspective of the universe.

78
00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:03.600
We are made of the same atoms we are
trying

79
00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.240
to measure, and we are held by the same
gravity

80
00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.680
we are trying to map.

81
00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.880
The observer is an integrated part of the
system.

82
00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:14.080
This suggests that the contradictions in
our physics might be

83
00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:16.160
a result of our own position.

84
00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:18.960
We are matter attempting to model the laws
that allow

85
00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:22.800
us to exist, the universe using its own
internal logic

86
00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:25.280
to finally describe itself.

